+- **When not to use**: Dense volumes where the overhead of table lookups outweighs the benefit of skipping; dynamic data where table construction cost is prohibitive.
 
 ## Background
-Hierarchical Grid Traversal, also known as Ray-Mipmap Traversal, is a technique for accelerating volume rendering by utilizing multi-resolution grid structures. It builds on the principles of ray-grid traversal [17-ray-grid-traversal.md] and hierarchical data structures [4392-hierarchical-and-block-based-data-structures.md]. The method is implemented in open-source projects such as [Jax-Volumetric-Renderer](https://github.com/szat/Jax-Volumetric-Renderer) [S1, unofficial] and [HNanoSolver](https://github.com/ZephirFXEC/HNanoSolver) [S2, unofficial]. The concept of partitioning volumes and using hierarchical structures for visibility culling has been explored in academic literature, such as the work by Li et al. on KD-Tree partitioned volume rendering [S3, unofficial].
+Hierarchical Grid Traversal is a method for accelerating ray traversal in volume rendering by using a multi-resolution grid hierarchy (mipmap) [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial]. It is closely related to Hierarchical Digital Differential Analyzer (HDDA) and other hierarchical traversal techniques. The method is implemented in projects such as Jax-Volumetric-Renderer [S1, unofficial] and HNanoSolver [S2, unofficial]. Variants include Grid Sphere Traversal for SDF grids [S4, unofficial] and KD-Tree Partitioned Volume Rendering for transfer-function-based partitioning [S3, unofficial].
 
